      "content": "#include <cassert>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#include <omp.h>\n#endif\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    if (std::scanf(\"%d %d\", &n, &s) != 2) return 0;\n\n    assert(s < n);\n    assert(n < 8000);\n    assert(s > 0);\n    assert(n > 0);\n\n    const std::size_t row_width = static_cast<std::size_t>(n);\n    std::vector<int> matrix(row_width * row_width);\n    for (int r = 0; r < n; ++r) {\n        int* row = matrix.data() + static_cast<std::size_t>(r) * row_width;\n        for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\n            if (std::scanf(\"%d\", &row[c]) != 1) return 0;\n        }\n    }\n\n    const int window_count = n - s + 1;\n    long long max_sum = LLONG_MIN;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel reduction(max:max_sum)\n    {\n        int team_size = 1;\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n        team_size = omp_get_num_threads();\n#endif\n\n        // Each statically assigned block owns a contiguous range of top rows.\n        #pragma omp for schedule(static, 1)\n        for (int block = 0; block < team_size; ++block) {\n            const int first = static_cast<int>(\n                static_cast<long long>(window_count) * block / team_size);\n            const int last = static_cast<int>(\n                static_cast<long long>(window_count) * (block + 1) / team_size);\n\n            if (first < last) {\n                std::vector<long long> vertical(row_width, 0);\n\n                // Initialize the S-row vertical sums for this block's first row.\n                for (int r = first; r < first + s; ++r) {\n                    const int* row = matrix.data() +\n                                     static_cast<std::size_t>(r) * row_width;\n                    for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\n                        vertical[static_cast<std::size_t>(c)] += row[c];\n                    }\n                }\n\n                for (int top = first; top < last; ++top) {\n                    if (top > first) {\n                        const int* leaving = matrix.data() +\n                            static_cast<std::size_t>(top - 1) * row_width;\n                        const int* entering = matrix.data() +\n                            static_cast<std::size_t>(top + s - 1) * row_width;\n                        for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\n                            vertical[static_cast<std::size_t>(c)] +=\n                                static_cast<long long>(entering[c]) - leaving[c];\n                        }\n                    }\n\n                    long long sum = 0;\n                    for (int c = 0; c < s; ++c) {\n                        sum += vertical[static_cast<std::size_t>(c)];\n                    }\n                    if (sum > max_sum) max_sum = sum;\n\n                    for (int left = 1; left < window_count; ++left) {\n                        sum += vertical[static_cast<std::size_t>(left + s - 1)] -\n                               vertical[static_cast<std::size_t>(left - 1)];\n                        if (sum > max_sum) max_sum = sum;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", max_sum);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Balanced contiguous blocks of top-row windows let each OpenMP thread reuse a private, full-width rolling-sum vector across its block. Static work sharing and a max reduction should retain O(N²) scan work while improving row-major locality and amortizing each thread's initial S-row setup.",
  "notes": "One source-only candidate; the OpenMP team size controls the number of blocks, and each active thread uses O(N) scratch. No benchmark-specific size assumptions are added.",
